                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c190739e-b74f-3712-9da1-4e251affd9a1",
                        "entry_id": "a7196156-0aad-3a38-8f71-0baa31c35bfb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "матем. связанный, соотносящийся по значению с существительным экспонента; изменяющийся по экспоненте (показательной функции)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd817a7d-5c5e-476b-ba86-da8bb82380ec",
                                "sense_id": "c190739e-b74f-3712-9da1-4e251affd9a1",
                                "text": "Плотность и давление воздуха с высотой уменьшаются примерно по экспоненциальному закону."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "62dd4195-c99d-468c-a8fe-3f721e178549",
                        "source_entry_id": "a7196156-0aad-3a38-8f71-0baa31c35bfb",
                        "source_sense_id": "c190739e-b74f-3712-9da1-4e251affd9a1",
                        "target_lang_word": "exponential",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exponential",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb8b3be2-c793-3f41-8d7b-29f637562a39",
                                        "entry_id": "3438f1ff-bb11-3a4c-8176-0a9dbb03abcf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating to an exponent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2fee3fbe-c8d2-3dfb-bfc9-8774f492e2ed",
                                        "entry_id": "3438f1ff-bb11-3a4c-8176-0a9dbb03abcf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Expressed in terms of an exponent (power of a base), the base often being 10 or e."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8c2f780-e6c8-4ac3-974a-9dd5e5a70ff0",
                                                "sense_id": "2fee3fbe-c8d2-3dfb-bfc9-8774f492e2ed",
                                                "text": "In base-10 exponential form, 1,000,000 is written as 10⁶."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57558d53-0602-4ca4-9987-7380936c6591",
                                                "sense_id": "2fee3fbe-c8d2-3dfb-bfc9-8774f492e2ed",
                                                "text": "If not otherwise specified, \"the\" exponential function is normally understood to mean eˣ."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "836b8c42-8ec1-379c-83b0-1a79a5062904",
                                        "entry_id": "3438f1ff-bb11-3a4c-8176-0a9dbb03abcf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Characterised by a rate of change that is proportional to the value of the varying quantity, or, equivalently, by a doubling or halving over successive fixed intervals of time or other parameter, described as exponential growth or exponential decay."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "644a974d-ec86-43c4-b39c-0ed275e2bb66",
                                                "sense_id": "836b8c42-8ec1-379c-83b0-1a79a5062904",
                                                "text": "There were two deaths on Monday, four on Tuesday, and eight on Wednesday. The rate of increase seems exponential."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ed8e7b8-b6b7-4939-9411-ccb90ebdae4e",
                                                "sense_id": "836b8c42-8ec1-379c-83b0-1a79a5062904",
                                                "text": "... Students apply the definition of slope to various representations of growth functions to discover differences between exponential and constant rate of growth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2cf9ab8c-2df2-3703-833c-f24b23729dc7",
                                        "entry_id": "3438f1ff-bb11-3a4c-8176-0a9dbb03abcf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Characterised by a very rapid rate of change, especially increase, or merely a very large amount or degree."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd4612fd-4dad-4b59-8878-3ff786b3c435",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf9ab8c-2df2-3703-833c-f24b23729dc7",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: extreme, huge"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d3065b7-7463-49b5-9c30-1ad82f683f63",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf9ab8c-2df2-3703-833c-f24b23729dc7",
                                                "text": "There's been an exponential rise in the number of crimes reported this year, compared to last year."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ad5c11c-4396-40a4-98bc-7b76c83515ef",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf9ab8c-2df2-3703-833c-f24b23729dc7",
                                                "text": "If loans are not what you are looking for, then search for scholarships [...] I have been putting together scholarship letters for parents over the past decade, and there is an exponential amount of money to be had."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5484ec05-952a-4863-a53b-05e9a866f055",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf9ab8c-2df2-3703-833c-f24b23729dc7",
                                                "text": "It is also about an arms control forum that has been meeting just once every five years for decision making on topics that are moving with exponential velocity [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee359d51-82c4-4b70-b791-645493b6ba48",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf9ab8c-2df2-3703-833c-f24b23729dc7",
                                                "text": "Of course, one can creatively conjure up a host of things robot-politicians can do at exponential speed and scale, from shaking hands and kissing babies to handling the fundraising “robocalls” that frustrate American voters."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "exponential",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e429bba-2e58-37ab-8416-035e5075329c",
                                        "entry_id": "ff956607-b2ed-375b-96ec-b398ba79a661",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any function that has an exponent as an independent variable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
